# Every text file is checked out with LF, whatever a machine's core.autocrlf says
# (Git for Windows defaults it to true, which would give CRLF). Git still detects
# binary files itself, so images and archives are untouched.
#
# Three things break on CRLF:
# - migrations are checksummed byte for byte (scripts/db-migrations-core.mjs)
#   and the ledger holds the LF checksums, so a CRLF checkout reports every
#   applied migration as drifted and `db:migrate` refuses to run;
# - bash cannot run a script with CRLF line endings ("$'\r': command not found");
# - Prettier's default `endOfLine` is lf, so `npm run prettier` flags every
#   CRLF file and `npm run format` rewrites it.
* text=auto eol=lf
